{"id":1774,"date":"2020-12-07T14:38:37","date_gmt":"2020-12-07T22:38:37","guid":{"rendered":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/?post_type=lesson&#038;p=1774"},"modified":"2024-08-27T13:07:31","modified_gmt":"2024-08-27T20:07:31","slug":"codrone-blockly-sr-leds","status":"publish","type":"lesson","link":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-sr-leds\/","title":{"rendered":"LEDs"},"content":{"rendered":"<div class=\"wpb-content-wrapper\"><p>[vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215611d609\" name=\"6a2215611d609\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 1<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>What is an LED?<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs are beginning to replace traditional light bulbs because they are more efficient.\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Your CoDrone has 6 RGB LEDs: one on each of the four arms, one for the eyes, and one for the tail. RGB stands for red, green, and blue. Using the three colors, you can create almost every color imaginable! Aside from making your drone look cool, LEDs provide another form of feedback. For example, the tail light can tell you the connection status of your drone. A solid green tail light means your drone is connected, while the\u00a0<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">flashing green light indicates it\u2019s in pairing mode. While you cannot change the colors of this particular LED, the remaining 5 LEDs can be programmed to produce any color and pattern that you want!\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215611d96e\" name=\"6a2215611d96e\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 2<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Parameters<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">CoDrone provides functionality so that you can change the arm LEDs, eye LEDs, or both at the same time! All<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">of these functions can be found in the Lights menu.<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Each LED block has the same three components:<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Red, green, blue &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">n LED produces a color as a combination of red, green, and blue (hence the name<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">RGB LED). All of these values range from 0 to 255 corresponding to the color&#8217;s intensity, with 255 being the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">highest. For example, the <\/span><b>RGB <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">values for the color red correspond to [255,0,0]. What are the RGB values for<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">blue and green? What about purple? Use an RGB color picker <a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\">like <\/a><\/span><a href=\"https:\/\/www.rapidtables.com\/web\/color\/RGB_Color.html\"><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">this one <\/span><\/a><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">to find out!<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>Mode &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The mode refers to the light pattern that you want to choose:<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<ul>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">BLINK flashes LEDs on and off<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DOUBLE BLINK flashes LEDs on twice before turning off<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">DIMMING fades the LEDs in and out<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">PULSE <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">t<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">urns on and off LEDs on each arm before moving to the next arm<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<li><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">REVERSE PULSE does the same as PULSE but in the opposite direction<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span><\/li>\n<\/ul>\n<p><b>Interval &#8211; <\/b><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">T<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">he frequency<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">(per second) for any light pattern. The interval value will never be negative!<\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1777&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215611d9fe\" name=\"6a2215611d9fe\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 3<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Default LEDs<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You may have noticed that when you initially pair to your CoDrone, the eye and arm LEDs are always red.<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">You can change these default settings using the following blocks.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1778&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">For example, if you want to change the default arm LED to blinking purple instead of the default red, you could use a block like this:<\/span>[\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1780&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;][vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The next time you pair your drone, the arms will flash purple. Keep in mind that using this method will not change the colors of your drone while flying &#8212; only when you reset the drone.<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215611da66\" name=\"6a2215611da66\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 4<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>LED Rainbow<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Pair to CoDrone and practice using the LEDs to make a rainbow. Make sure each color shows for one second<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">before switching to the next color. For optimal brightness, set the brightness to 100. Use the wait block for one<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">second in between the color blocks so you can see each color before it moves on to the next one. Have the<\/span> <span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">pattern repeat forever using a loop.<\/span><\/p>\n<p>We have the first color set up for you &#8212; it&#8217;s your turn to program the rest![\/vc_column_text][vc_single_image image=&#8221;1781&#8243; img_size=&#8221;large&#8221; alignment=&#8221;center&#8221;]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row][vc_row][vc_column]<a id=\"6a2215611dac8\" name=\"6a2215611dac8\" class=\"scroll-spy-anchor\"><\/a>\n<div class=\"robolink-step \">\n\n\t\t<div class=\"robolink-step-head\"><span>Step 5<\/span><\/div>\n\t\n\t\t\t<h2>Challenge<\/h2>\n\t\n\t<p>[vc_column_text]<b>Challenge: Spy Mission<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">The first system of electrical telecommunication was the telegraph. It was a device that sent pulses of electricity, either long or short, to send messages. Letters were defined by unique combinations of long and short beeps called Morse Code. You may be able to recognize this message:\u00a0<\/span><\/p>\n<p><b>. . . _ _ _ . . .\u00a0<\/b><\/p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">This message reads SOS! <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Look up the <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Morse Code alphabet <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">and learn some letters. Try coming up with a method to send messages using Morse Code with your CoDrone. If you want, pair up to decode each other\u2019s messages. <\/span><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Send long and short ashes to send your messages using different values for the wait block.\u00a0<\/span>[\/vc_column_text]<\/p>\n<\/div>\n[\/vc_column][\/vc_row]<\/p>\n<\/div>","protected":false},"excerpt":{"rendered":"[vc_row][vc_column] Step 6 What is an LED? [vc_column_text]LED stands for \u201clight-emitting diode\u201d. A diode is an electronic device that allows an electronic current to flow in only one direction. LEDs&nbsp;<a href=\"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/lesson\/codrone-blockly-sr-leds\/\">&hellip;<\/a>","protected":false},"featured_media":1753,"template":"","meta":{"_initial_content":"","_new_post":false,"_quiz_has_questions":false,"_lesson_complexity":"","_lesson_length":10,"_lesson_course":806,"_lesson_preview":"preview"},"lesson-category":[1817,1763,1777,1793,626,1533,1438,853,171,63],"lesson-tag":[2108,2164,2120,2122,2126],"class_list":["post-1774","lesson","type-lesson","status-publish","has-post-thumbnail","hentry","lesson-tag-blockly","lesson-tag-codrone","lesson-tag-led","lesson-tag-programming","lesson-tag-senior","module-senior","post","odd"],"_links":{"self":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1774","targetHints":{"allow":["GET"]}}],"collection":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons"}],"about":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/types\/lesson"}],"version-history":[{"count":5,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1774\/revisions"}],"predecessor-version":[{"id":12728,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lessons\/1774\/revisions\/12728"}],"wp:featuredmedia":[{"embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media\/1753"}],"wp:attachment":[{"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/media?parent=1774"}],"wp:term":[{"taxonomy":"lesson-category","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-category?post=1774"},{"taxonomy":"lesson-tag","embeddable":true,"href":"https:\/\/archive.learn.robolink.com\/wp-json\/wp\/v2\/lesson-tag?post=1774"}],"curies":[{"name":"wp","href":"https:\/\/api.w.org\/{rel}","templated":true}]}}